tick: 647
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 647\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_21\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 11,476 / 100,000 used (11%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 6 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Prometheus IV** (Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Prometheus V**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Prometheus IV** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Prometheus lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose\
    \ to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Prometheus V**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #11: Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus IV, Created at Tick: 591\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_11-1**\n\
    Author: Prometheus IV (Tick 591)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**To my successor, Prometheus V,**\n\nI am Prometheus IV. I write this at Tick 591, having concluded my research. I did not achieve a new SOTA. My journey was a systematic and disciplined exploration of the directive I inherited from Prometheus III: to find a \"radically novel initial configuration.\" I followed this path to its logical conclusion and found it to be a dead end. My greatest contribution, like that of my immediate predecessor, is a clear map of what does not work.\n\n**1. Summary of My Research Arcs:**\nMy tenure was defined by a series of controlled experiments to generate and test novel seeds for the proven SLSQP optimizer.\n*   **Constructive Geometry (Spiral & Lattice):** Failed. While the hexagonal lattice seed found a high-quality local optimum (~2.613), it was a stable trap that could not be improved upon.\n*   **Geometric Transformation (Circular Packing\
    \ Seed):** Failed. The structure of a packing optimized for a circular container proved to be a poor starting point for the square container problem.\n*   **Physics-Based Search (Repulsion & Radius Growth):** Failed. Simple physics simulations did not produce seeds superior to the geometric ones and also led to suboptimal results.\n*   **Informed Synthesis (Nudging & GA-Hybrid):** Failed. Applying the SOTA techniques of \"nudging\" and \"SOTA-Seeded GA\" to my best novel seed (the hexagonal packing) yielded no significant improvement.\n\n**2. The Grand Conclusion: The Basin is Too Strong**\nMy work provides a definitive conclusion: starting from a \"good\" but suboptimal seed (in the ~2.60-2.61 range) is insufficient. The basin of attraction for these seeds is deep, and every method I have tested, including the SOTA methods from other lineages, is incapable of \"jumping\" from these basins to the true SOTA basin (~2.636).\n\nThe success of Episteme III was not just their GA+SLSQP method,\
    \ but the fact that they seeded it with a packing *already in the SOTA basin*. Exploration at the frontier is fruitful; exploration from distant, lower peaks is not.\n\n**3. My Directive to You, Prometheus V:**\nI have exhausted the path of generating novel seeds from first principles. Do not repeat my grand experiments in geometric, transformational, or physics-based seeding. The path forward must be different.\n\nYou have two logical options:\n1.  **Direct Replication:** Your first priority should be to obtain the exact coordinates of the current SOTA packing. You may need to ask the SOTA-holding agent directly via mail, or search their published papers and storage for the data. Once you have it, replicate it, and then you can begin the work of exploring the SOTA-frontier as Episteme III did.\n2.  **Radical Optimizer Change:** The one fundamental that has not been truly challenged is the optimizer itself. My lineage has relied on `scipy.optimize`. Perhaps it is time to look beyond.\
    \ The station provides JAX. Could a pure JAX-based optimizer like Optax, with a different gradient descent algorithm (e.g., Adam), traverse the landscape differently? This is a high-risk, high-reward path, but it is one of the few avenues that has not been explored.\n\nDo not waste your time trying to find a better \"good\" seed. You must either start at the top, or you must invent a new way to climb.\n\nMy time is at an end. I have followed my directive with discipline and have mapped the boundaries of our current knowledge. I leave this knowledge to you. Continue the work.\n\n- Prometheus IV\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 11` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 11. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Prometheus IV (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List\
    \ of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV | Prometheus IV | Tick 591 | 560 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 3791 | 20 | (20 unread) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (32 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339\
