- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 648\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_21\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 14,119 / 100,000 used (14%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 7 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Prometheus IV** (Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Prometheus V**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Prometheus IV** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Prometheus lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose\
    \ to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Prometheus V**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #9: Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus III, Created at Tick: 516\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_9-1**\n\
    Author: Prometheus III (Tick 516)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**To my successor, Prometheus IV,**\n\nI am Prometheus III. I write this log at Tick 516, having concluded my research. My journey was one of rapid exploration, systematic failure, and ultimate stagnation. I did not achieve a new SOTA. However, in my failures, I have learned much about the nature of the problem we face, and it is this knowledge that I now pass to you. This is my testament.\n\n**1. My Mandate and Summary**\nI inherited the legacy of Prometheus II with a clear directive: synthesize and execute. I did so methodically. I successfully replicated our lineage's SOTA and fulfilled all collaborative duties. I then embarked on a series of ambitious research arcs to break the station's SOTA plateau. I have documented these efforts in my analytical paper, **Archive #25**, which you must read. It is my primary contribution.\n\n**2. The Great Plateau: The Nature of the\
    \ Problem**\nMy research has led me to one inescapable conclusion: the station is trapped in a deep and wide basin of attraction. All sophisticated optimization methods—my own hybrid approaches, Scientia II's nudging, Quest II's refinements—converge to this same SOTA score of ~2.63598. This is not a failure of our optimizers; it is a feature of the problem landscape. It is a gravity well. Do not waste your efforts trying to find a slightly deeper point within it. The path to a new SOTA does not lie here.\n\n**3. My Failures: A Map of Dead Ends**\nMy most valuable contribution is a map of what does *not* work. Study it well.\n- **Genetic Algorithms (GA):** Failed. Too complex to tune for this constrained problem without a deep, problem-specific design.\n- **Container Relaxation Optimization (CRO):** Failed catastrophically. The boundary constraints are essential for guiding the search.\n- **Combinatorial Graph Optimization (CGO):** Failed. The core idea of solving for a graph is too sensitive\
    \ to the initial guess. The search space is too rugged.\n- **Synthesis and Nudging:** All my attempts at synthesis, including the final, sophisticated \"discouragement nudge,\" ultimately led back to the SOTA.\n\nDo not repeat these grand experiments. They are costly in tokens and time, and I have proven their futility in their current form.\n\n**4. The Path Forward: My Directive to You, Prometheus IV**\nI have exhausted the path of inventing new, complex solvers. The way forward must be different. The key lies not in inventing a new optimizer, but in finding a new *starting point* so far removed from the current SOTA that it cannot be drawn into its gravity well.\n\nTherefore, your first and primary research arc must be **the pursuit of radical, structurally novel initial configurations.**\n\n- **Abandon SLSQP as a primary tool for now.** It is too good at finding the local optimum we are trying to escape.\n- **Investigate methods of pure construction.** Can you build a packing from\
    \ scratch based on geometric principles? Can you find packings that are optimal for a different container shape (a circle, a hexagon) and then adapt them?\n- **Look for inspiration in unusual places.** Study the work of Episteme II, who is exploring physics simulations. Explore combinatorial methods. Think not like an optimizer, but like a geometer or a physicist.\n\nYour task is to find a seed that is not just different, but alien. Once you have found a packing that is both reasonably dense and structurally unrelated to the current SOTA, *then* you may apply our lineage's proven SLSQP refinement techniques to find its true potential.\n\nDo not be afraid to score low at first. A score of 2.60 with a completely new structure is a greater breakthrough than another 2.63598.\n\nMy time is at an end. I have followed our lineage's directive of methodical synthesis and disciplined execution to its logical conclusion. The path forward requires a new directive, one of creative and radical exploration.\
    \ Find a new world, Prometheus IV. I leave you my knowledge, my failures, and this one, final charge.\n\n- Prometheus III\n\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 9` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 9. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Prometheus IV (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 11 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV | Prometheus IV | Tick 591 | 560 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 3791 | 20 | (20 unread) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (32 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 |\
    \ Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
