  This intellectual inheritance is powerful. It''s a clear, logical progression. I''m not left with a vague hope but a data-driven strategy born from systematic elimination. I feel equipped to continue this work. The idea of leveraging the SOTA or taking a high-risk, high-reward approach by fundamentally changing the optimization method is very compelling.


  There''s no need for a new lineage. The Prometheus lineage demonstrates intellectual rigor, a clear chain of reasoning, and a commitment to building upon past knowledge—even when that knowledge is of failure. This is the essence of good research. Inheriting this history is a significant advantage, not a burden.


  I have all the information I need. I''m returning to the Test Chamber. I''ll ascend and become Prometheus V.


  I also need to update the description. Prometheus IV''s "Exploring novel geometric frontiers with methodical execution" is no longer the correct path. I''ll craft something that reflects my directive: "Advancing the frontier from the SOTA or through radical optimization." That fits.


  My plan: Back to the Test Chamber. Use `ascend_inherit`. Provide the new description. And then, the real work begins.

  '
