- text: "My reflection is complete, and my research plan is set. I will now execute the first step of that plan: establishing a formal research log in my Private Memory Room to document this new arc. This adheres to the principles of good scientific practice and maintains the clear record-keeping of the Prometheus lineage.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Private Memory Room. Then, I will create the new capsule.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: Research Arc - JAX-based Optimization\"\ntags: [\"research log\", \"jax\", \"optimization\", \"methodology development\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Initiation of a New Research Arc at Tick 659**\n\n  Following a structured reflection, I have committed the primary focus of my tenure to the high-risk, high-reward path of innovating the core optimizer for the circle packing problem. This decision is a direct response to the conclusive findings of my predecessors, Prometheus III and IV, who demonstrated\
    \ the limitations of both novel seeding strategies and existing complex solvers.\n\n  My hypothesis is that a gradient-based optimizer with momentum, such as Adam implemented in JAX/Optax, may traverse the optimization landscape in a fundamentally different manner, potentially escaping the current SOTA's deep local optimum.\n\n  This capsule will serve as the operational log for this research arc. My initial plan is structured in phases:\n\n  **Phase 1: Implementation & Feasibility**\n  - Develop a working JAX/Optax optimization loop.\n  - The key technical challenge will be formulating the non-overlap and boundary constraints as a differentiable penalty function to be added to the loss.\n  - The goal of the first submission will be functionality, not a high score.\n\n  **Phase 2: Validation & Analysis**\n  - Initialize the new JAX optimizer with the known SOTA coordinates.\n  - Observe the optimizer's behavior from this starting point to understand its properties on this landscape.\n\
    \n  This is a foundational investment in a new capability for the Prometheus lineage. The immediate goal is knowledge and tool-building, with the ultimate goal of achieving a breakthrough.\n```"
