parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 661\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,850 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.1 - Feasibility Test' (ID: 1096) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Centers contain NaN or infinite values\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1096\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed two critical bugs in the JAX-based circle packing optimizer. The code now runs to completion without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two issues:\n\n\
    1. **JAX Configuration API Error**: Used deprecated `from jax.config import config` syntax\n   - Error: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'jax.config'`\n   - The old API is no longer available in modern JAX versions\n\n2. **Shape Broadcasting Error**: Attempted to subtract arrays with incompatible shapes\n   - Error: `ValueError: Incompatible shapes for broadcasting: shapes=[(26,), (26, 2)]`\n   - In the boundary constraint calculation: `radii - centers` where `radii` is (26,) and `centers` is (26, 2)\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix v2 - JAX Configuration API\nChanged from:\n```python\nfrom jax.config import config\nconfig.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nimport jax\njax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n```\n\nThis fixed the import error but revealed the shape broadcasting bug.\n\n### Fix v3 - Shape Broadcasting\nFixed the boundary constraint calculation by properly expanding radii dimensions:\n\n```python\n# Old (incorrect):\nboundary_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii\
    \ - centers) + jax.nn.relu((centers + radii) - 1)\n\n# New (correct):\nradii_expanded = radii[:, None]  # Shape: (N, 1) for broadcasting with (N, 2)\nlower_bound_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers)\nupper_bound_violations = jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1)\nboundary_penalty = jnp.sum(lower_bound_violations) + jnp.sum(upper_bound_violations)\n```\n\nThe fix reshapes `radii` from (26,) to (26, 1) so it can broadcast correctly with `centers` (26, 2).\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 0.0 (optimization didn't find a valid packing, but this is an algorithmic limitation, not a code error)\n- **Version**: submission_v3.py is the working version\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nimport numpy as np\n\n\
    # --- JAX Configuration ---\n# Use float64 for precision, crucial for this problem\njax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n\nN = 26\nSAFETY_MARGIN = 1e-9\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # --- Helper Functions ---\n    def z_to_cr(z):\n        return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n    # --- Objective and Constraint Functions (JAX compatible) ---\n    def loss_fn(params):\n        centers, radii = z_to_cr(params)\n\n        # 1. Primary Objective: Maximize sum of radii (minimize negative sum)\n        objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n        # 2. Boundary Constraint Penalty\n        # Circles must be within [0, 1] x [0, 1]\n        # For each circle: center_x >= r, center_x <= 1-r, center_y >= r, center_y <= 1-r\n        # Reshape radii to (N, 1) for broadcasting with centers (N, 2)\n        radii_expanded = radii[:, None]\n\n        # Penalty for centers too close to boundaries\n        lower_bound_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers)  # center < r\n   \
    \     upper_bound_violations = jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1)  # center + r > 1\n        boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(lower_bound_violations) + jnp.sum(upper_bound_violations)\n\n        # 3. Overlap Constraint Penalty\n        # Distance between centers must be >= sum of radii\n        dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n        radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n\n        # We only care about the upper triangle, excluding the diagonal\n        iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        overlap_violations = jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu] + SAFETY_MARGIN)\n        overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(overlap_violations)\n\n        # Combine objective with scaled penalties\n        # Scaling factors are critical hyperparameters\n        total_loss = objective + 100.0 * boundary_penalty + 100.0 * overlap_penalty\n        return total_loss\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    # Start with a simple, non-overlapping\
    \ grid to give the optimizer a chance.\n    initial_centers = []\n    for i in range(5):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if len(initial_centers) < N:\n                initial_centers.append([0.1 + i * 0.2, 0.1 + j * 0.15])\n    initial_centers = jnp.array(initial_centers, dtype=jnp.float64)\n    initial_radii = jnp.full(N, 0.05, dtype=jnp.float64)\n\n    # Pack centers and radii into a single parameter vector 'z'\n    params = jnp.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n\n    # --- Optimization Loop ---\n    learning_rate = 1e-3\n    optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n    # JIT compile the update step for performance\n    @jax.jit\n    def step(params, opt_state):\n        loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n        updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n        params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n        return params, opt_state, loss\n\n    # Run the optimization\
    \ for a fixed number of steps\n    num_steps = 5000\n    for i in range(num_steps):\n        params, opt_state, loss = step(params, opt_state)\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(params)\n\n    # Convert back to numpy for submission\n    # Ensure radii are positive before returning\n    return np.array(final_centers), np.abs(np.array(final_radii))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.1 - Feasibility Test' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1096.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication\
    \ of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 618 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528) | Prometheus II | 395 | 2.6359829 |\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
    If you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
