tick: 665
role: model
parts:
- text: "My research log is updated. Now I will implement the planned stability improvements. This involves modifying my utility script, `optimizer_v0_1.py`, to create a new, more robust version. I will then immediately test it, once again using the SOTA-seeded approach, as this provides the most sensitive test for stability near the optimum.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter.\nSecond, I will write the new, more stable optimizer to my storage as `optimizer_v0_2.py`.\nThird, I will submit the experiment that uses this new version.\n\nThe key changes in `optimizer_v0_2.py` will be:\n1.  Adding a small epsilon (`1e-12`) inside the `jnp.sqrt` calculation to prevent `NaN` gradients.\n2.  Using `optax.chain` to combine the `adam` optimizer with `optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0)` to cap the magnitude of gradient updates.\n\nThis is a focused, engineering-driven response to the experimental data.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write storage/Prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v0_2.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Filename: optimizer_v0_2.py\n  # Author: Prometheus V\n  # Date: Tick 665\n  # Description: A more robust JAX/Optax optimizer for circle packing.\n  # Version 0.2 incorporates gradient clipping and a safe square root\n  # to prevent NaN values and improve stability.\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  jax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY_MARGIN = 1e-9\n  SQRT_EPSILON = 1e-12 # Added for numerical stability\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def loss_fn(params):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n      radii_expanded = radii[:, None]\n      boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers) + jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1))\n\n      # MODIFICATION: Added SQRT_EPSILON for stability\n      dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1) + SQRT_EPSILON\n\
    \      dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq)\n      \n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu] + SAFETY_MARGIN))\n\n      total_loss = objective + 100.0 * boundary_penalty + 100.0 * overlap_penalty\n      return total_loss\n\n  def run_optimizer(initial_params, num_steps=3000, learning_rate=1e-4):\n      # MODIFICATION: Chained optimizer with gradient clipping\n      optimizer = optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Cap the gradient norm at 1.0\n          optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      )\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(initial_params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def step(params, opt_state):\n          loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, loss\n\n      params\
    \ = initial_params\n      for _ in range(num_steps):\n          params, opt_state, _ = step(params, opt_state)\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      return np.array(final_centers), np.abs(np.array(final_radii))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.3 - Stability Test (Clipping + Epsilon)\"\ntags: [\"jax\", \"optax\", \"gradient clipping\", \"stability\", \"sota-seeded\"]\nabstract: |\n  Third iteration of the JAX optimizer. This version directly addresses the NaN failures observed in previous experiments (1096, 1101). It introduces two standard stability enhancements: gradient clipping (via optax.clip_by_global_norm) and a safe square root calculation (adding an epsilon). The experiment is again seeded with the SOTA configuration to provide a stringent test of whether these changes prevent divergence.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/Prometheus/jax_utils')\n\
    \  # Use the new, more stable optimizer script\n  from optimizer_v0_2 import run_optimizer\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load SOTA data. {e}\")\n          return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if sota_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      initial_params = jnp.concatenate([\n          jnp.array(sota_centers.flatten(), dtype=jnp.float64),\n          jnp.array(sota_radii, dtype=jnp.float64)\n      ])\n      \n      # Using the robust optimizer\n      final_centers, final_radii = run_optimizer(initial_params)\n      \n      return\
    \ final_centers, final_radii\n```"
