tick: 667
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log is updated. The path forward is clear. I will now implement and test the first hyperparameter adjustment to my stable JAX optimizer.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter, create an `optimizer_v0_3.py` script with a 10x stronger overlap penalty, and then submit an experiment using it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write storage/Prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v0_3.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Filename: optimizer_v0_3.py\n  # Author: Prometheus V\n  # Date: Tick 667\n  # Description: First tuning iteration of the stable JAX optimizer.\n  # Version 0.3 increases the overlap penalty multiplier by 10x (from 100 to 1000)\n  # to more aggressively enforce the non-overlap constraint.\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  jax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY_MARGIN = 1e-9\n  SQRT_EPSILON = 1e-12\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def loss_fn(params):\n\
    \      centers, radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n      radii_expanded = radii[:, None]\n      boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers) + jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1))\n\n      dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1) + SQRT_EPSILON\n      dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq)\n      \n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      overlap_violations = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu] + SAFETY_MARGIN))\n\n      # MODIFICATION: Increased penalty for overlaps\n      total_loss = objective + 100.0 * boundary_penalty + 1000.0 * overlap_violations\n      return total_loss\n\n  def run_optimizer(initial_params, num_steps=3000, learning_rate=1e-4):\n      optimizer = optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      )\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(initial_params)\n\n\
    \      @jax.jit\n      def step(params, opt_state):\n          loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, loss\n\n      params = initial_params\n      for _ in range(num_steps):\n          params, opt_state, _ = step(params, opt_state)\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      return np.array(final_centers), np.abs(np.array(final_radii))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.4 - Tuning (Increased Overlap Penalty)\"\ntags: [\"jax\", \"optax\", \"tuning\", \"penalty method\", \"sota-seeded\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment begins the tuning phase for the stable JAX optimizer. Based on the minor overlap failure in the previous run (1106), this version increases the overlap penalty multiplier in the loss function by a factor of 10 (from 100 to\
    \ 1000). The goal is to produce a fully valid packing by more strongly discouraging circle overlaps. The experiment is again seeded with the SOTA configuration.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/Prometheus/jax_utils')\n  # Use the new optimizer script with the stronger penalty\n  from optimizer_v0_3 import run_optimizer\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load SOTA data. {e}\")\n          return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if sota_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)),\
    \ np.zeros(N)\n\n      initial_params = jnp.concatenate([\n          jnp.array(sota_centers.flatten(), dtype=jnp.float64),\n          jnp.array(sota_radii, dtype=jnp.float64)\n      ])\n      \n      # Using the robust, tuned optimizer\n      final_centers, final_radii = run_optimizer(initial_params)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
