- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 670\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 67,162 / 300,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 29 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.5 - Tuning (LR Schedule + Logging)' (ID: 1117) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circle 0 at (0.08326449454632383, 0.08707413499869919) with radius 0.08369068222320221 is outside the unit square\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1117\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the JAX gradient computation bug. The code now runs without crashing and completes\
    \ the full optimization process.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bug was in the `optimizer_v0_4.py` file from the agent's lineage directory at line 62:\n\n```python\ngrad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(lambda p: loss_fn(p)[0], has_aux=True)\n```\n\n**The Problem:**\n- `loss_fn(params)` returns a tuple: `(total_loss, metrics_dict)`\n- The lambda function `lambda p: loss_fn(p)[0]` extracts only the first element (the scalar `total_loss`)\n- However, `has_aux=True` tells JAX that the function should return a 2-element tuple `(value, aux)`\n- Since the lambda returns only a scalar (not a tuple), JAX raised a `TypeError`\n\n**The Error Message:**\n```\nTypeError: expected function with aux output to return a two-element tuple,\nbut got type <class 'jax._src.interpreters.ad.JVPTracer'> with value\nTraced<ShapedArray(float64[])>\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 62 from:\n```python\ngrad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(lambda p: loss_fn(p)[0], has_aux=True)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\ngrad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn,\
    \ has_aux=True)\n```\n\n**Why This Works:**\n- Now `jax.value_and_grad` receives the full `loss_fn` function\n- `loss_fn` correctly returns `(total_loss, metrics_dict)` as a 2-element tuple\n- JAX properly handles this with `has_aux=True`, returning `((loss, metrics), grads)`\n- The optimizer can now extract both the loss value and the auxiliary metrics dictionary\n\n## Results\n**Version v2 Evaluation:**\n- ✅ Code executes without Python errors\n- ✅ All 5000 optimization steps complete successfully\n- ✅ Loss metrics are logged every 500 steps as intended\n- ⚠️ Verification failed: One circle slightly outside unit square bounds\n\n**Important Note:**\nThe verification failure is NOT a code bug - it's a mathematical convergence issue. The optimizer didn't find a perfectly valid packing, but the code itself runs correctly. The agent may need to:\n- Adjust hyperparameters (learning rate, decay rate, num_steps)\n- Increase penalty weights for boundary violations\n- Improve the initial seed\
    \ configuration\n\nThe debugging task is **complete** - the code no longer crashes.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax\nimport optax\n\nN = 26\nSAFETY_MARGIN = 1e-9\nSQRT_EPSILON = 1e-12\n\njax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef loss_fn(params):\n    centers, radii = z_to_cr(params)\n\n    # Objective\n    objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n    # Penalties\n    radii_expanded = radii[:, None]\n    boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers) + jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1))\n\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1) + SQRT_EPSILON\n    dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq)\n    radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n\
    \    iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu] + SAFETY_MARGIN))\n\n    total_loss = objective + 100.0 * boundary_penalty + 1000.0 * overlap_penalty\n\n    # Return a dictionary for logging\n    return total_loss, {\n        \"total_loss\": total_loss,\n        \"objective\": objective,\n        \"boundary_penalty\": boundary_penalty,\n        \"overlap_penalty\": overlap_penalty,\n    }\n\ndef run_optimizer(initial_params, num_steps=5000, initial_lr=1e-3, decay_rate=0.999):\n    # Exponential decay learning rate schedule\n    schedule = optax.exponential_decay(\n        init_value=initial_lr,\n        transition_steps=100,\n        decay_rate=decay_rate\n    )\n\n    optimizer = optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=schedule)\n    )\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(initial_params)\n\n    # FIX: Changed from `lambda p: loss_fn(p)[0]` to `loss_fn`\n    # The issue was that\
    \ loss_fn returns (loss, metrics) tuple,\n    # and we need to pass the whole function to value_and_grad with has_aux=True\n    grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def step(params, opt_state):\n        (loss, metrics), grads = grad_fn(params)\n        updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n        params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n        return params, opt_state, metrics\n\n    params = initial_params\n    for i in range(num_steps):\n        params, opt_state, metrics = step(params, opt_state)\n        if i % 500 == 0:\n            print(\n                f\"Step {i:04d}: \"\n                f\"Loss={metrics['total_loss']:.4f}, \"\n                f\"Objective={metrics['objective']:.4f}, \"\n                f\"BoundaryPen={metrics['boundary_penalty']:.4e}, \"\n                f\"OverlapPen={metrics['overlap_penalty']:.4e}\"\n            )\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(params)\n    return np.array(final_centers),\
    \ np.abs(np.array(final_radii))\n\ndef load_sota_data():\n    centers_path = 'storage/prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n    radii_path = 'storage/prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load SOTA data. {e}\")\n        return None, None\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    sota_centers, sota_radii = load_sota_data()\n    if sota_centers is None:\n        return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    initial_params = jnp.concatenate([\n        jnp.array(sota_centers.flatten(), dtype=jnp.float64),\n        jnp.array(sota_radii, dtype=jnp.float64)\n    ])\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = run_optimizer(initial_params)\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStep 0000: Loss=-2.6360, Objective=-2.6360, BoundaryPen=0.0000e+00,\
    \ OverlapPen=0.0000e+00\nStep 0500: Loss=-2.4339, Objective=-2.5871, BoundaryPen=2.1476e-04, OverlapPen=1.3174e-04\nStep 1000: Loss=-2.5555, Objective=-2.5901, BoundaryPen=0.0000e+00, OverlapPen=3.4647e-05\nStep 1500: Loss=-2.5114, Objective=-2.5835, BoundaryPen=2.1366e-04, OverlapPen=5.0639e-05\nStep 2000: Loss=-2.5297, Objective=-2.5855, BoundaryPen=2.6000e-04, OverlapPen=2.9770e-05\nStep 2500: Loss=-1.6319, Objective=-2.5885, BoundaryPen=8.7911e-04, OverlapPen=8.6867e-04\nStep 3000: Loss=-2.3511, Objective=-2.5908, BoundaryPen=2.0416e-04, OverlapPen=2.1928e-04\nStep 3500: Loss=-2.5785, Objective=-2.5785, BoundaryPen=0.0000e+00, OverlapPen=0.0000e+00\nStep 4000: Loss=-2.4004, Objective=-2.5853, BoundaryPen=1.0282e-04, OverlapPen=1.7465e-04\nStep 4500: Loss=-2.5896, Objective=-2.5896, BoundaryPen=0.0000e+00, OverlapPen=0.0000e+00\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage write storage/Prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v0_4.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v0_4.py\n- Evaluation 'Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v0.5 - Tuning (LR Schedule + Logging)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1117.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA\
    \ Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 618 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528) | Prometheus II | 395 | 2.6359829 |\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12)\
    \ | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
