- text: "With my plan updated, I will now execute the fine-tuning experiment. This involves creating a final, polished version of my optimizer utility script and then using it in a submission with carefully chosen hyperparameters.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter.\nSecond, I will write the corrected and parameterized optimizer to `storage/Prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v1_0.py`, marking a major version change.\nThird, I will submit the experiment with a low learning rate and an increased boundary penalty.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write storage/Prometheus/jax_utils/optimizer_v1_0.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Filename: optimizer_v1_0.py\n  # Author: Prometheus V\n  # Date: Tick 671\n  # Description: First production-ready JAX optimizer.\n  # Version 1.0 incorporates the critical bug fix from the station debugger (ID 1117),\n  # parameterizes penalty weights, and includes diagnostic logging.\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import\
    \ optax\n  import numpy as np\n\n  jax.config.update(\"jax_enable_x64\", True)\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY_MARGIN = 1e-9\n  SQRT_EPSILON = 1e-12\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def loss_fn(params, boundary_weight, overlap_weight):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n      radii_expanded = radii[:, None]\n      boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_expanded - centers) + jax.nn.relu((centers + radii_expanded) - 1))\n      \n      dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1) + SQRT_EPSILON\n      dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq)\n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      iu = jnp.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu] + SAFETY_MARGIN))\n\n      total_loss = objective + boundary_weight * boundary_penalty + overlap_weight * overlap_penalty\n\n      return total_loss, {\n          \"total_loss\"\
    : total_loss,\n          \"objective\": objective,\n          \"boundary_penalty\": boundary_penalty,\n          \"overlap_penalty\": overlap_penalty,\n      }\n\n  def run_optimizer(initial_params, num_steps=5000, initial_lr=1e-5, decay_rate=0.999,\n                    boundary_weight=200.0, overlap_weight=1000.0):\n      \n      schedule = optax.exponential_decay(init_value=initial_lr, transition_steps=100, decay_rate=decay_rate)\n      optimizer = optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=schedule))\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(initial_params)\n      \n      # Corrected grad_fn based on debugger report for Eval 1117\n      grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(lambda p: loss_fn(p, boundary_weight, overlap_weight), has_aux=True)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def step(params, opt_state):\n          (loss, metrics), grads = grad_fn(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n\
    \          return params, opt_state, metrics\n\n      params = initial_params\n      for i in range(num_steps):\n          params, opt_state, metrics = step(params, opt_state)\n          if i % 1000 == 0:\n              print(f\"Step {i:04d}: Loss={metrics['total_loss']:.6f}, Objective={metrics['objective']:.6f}, \"\n                    f\"BoundaryPen={metrics['boundary_penalty']:.4e}, OverlapPen={metrics['overlap_penalty']:.4e}\")\n              \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(params)\n      return np.array(final_centers), np.abs(np.array(final_radii))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v1.1 - Fine-Tuning (Low LR)\"\ntags: [\"jax\", \"optax\", \"tuning\", \"lr-schedule\", \"sota-seeded\", \"production\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment uses the first production-ready version of the JAX optimizer (v1.0), which includes the debugger's critical fix. Based on analysis of logs from run 1117, this submission uses a much lower initial\
    \ learning rate (1e-5) to prevent the optimizer from being \"kicked\" out of the optimal basin. The boundary penalty is also increased. The goal is to achieve the first high-scoring, valid packing from the JAX optimizer.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/Prometheus/jax_utils')\n  from optimizer_v1_0 import run_optimizer\n\n  N = 26\n  \n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers, radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load SOTA data. {e}\")\n          return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      sota_centers, sota_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if sota_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\
    \n      initial_params = jnp.concatenate([\n          jnp.array(sota_centers.flatten(), dtype=jnp.float64),\n          jnp.array(sota_radii, dtype=jnp.float64)\n      ])\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = run_optimizer(\n          initial_params,\n          initial_lr=1e-5, # Drastically reduced learning rate\n          boundary_weight=500.0, # Increased boundary penalty\n          overlap_weight=1000.0\n      )\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
