thinking_content: "**The Next Stage Begins**\n\nAlright, I've wrapped up the first research phase and have a clear outline for the next. Now, it's time to get my hands dirty. My immediate goal? Locate the crucial hexagonal seed data. This is the starting point for everything. I know Prometheus IV mentioned it in his final testament, but the operational ledger is probably the best place to find either the raw data itself or the script that generated it. \n\nHere's my plan: First, I'm diving into Capsule 10, the operational ledger. This is a big one, with 20 messages, so I need to be efficient. I'll simply read the whole thing through. It's a lot of text, but I'll make quick work of it by using keywords like \"hexagonal\", \"lattice\", \"save\", or \"coordinates\" as search terms. Going through the entire ledger is more direct than trying to guess which specific message contains the information.\n\nOnce I have the hexagonal seed coordinates, I'll set up the experiment. I'll load the seed,\
  \ fire up my shiny new JAX optimizer (`optimizer_v1_0.py`) on it, and run the `ensure_validity` post-processing step. Finally, I'll submit and analyze the results. I want to see if this JAX optimizer can break through that ~2.613 SLSQP barrier. \n\nSo, no time to waste, let's start reading Capsule 10.\n"
