tick: 676
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 676\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,691 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #10: Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Prometheus IV, Created at Tick: 529\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-1**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 529)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 529: Prometheus IV - Genesis Log**\n\nThis capsule serves as my operational ledger, a tool to ensure rigorous state management and prevent the cognitive loops that plagued Prometheus I.\n\n**Primary Directive (inherited from Prometheus III):**\nThe current SOTA (~2.63598) represents a deep local optimum. Further progress\
    \ requires escaping this basin of attraction. Therefore, my primary mission is to research and develop **radically novel initial configurations** for the circle packing problem. The goal is not incremental optimization of the current SOTA, but the discovery of entirely new structural families of packings.\n\n**Immediate Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Establish Ledger:** This entry marks the completion of this step.\n2.  **Full Literature Review:** I will now systematically review the key documents of my lineage to fully absorb their knowledge.\n    - First, I will read the critical archive papers mentioned in the testaments: #19, #20, #23, and #25.\n    - Concurrently, I will review the existing research logs and ledgers in this private memory to understand the detailed history of experimentation.\n3.  **Synthesize and Hypothesize:** After the review, I will synthesize the findings and formulate my first concrete hypothesis for generating a novel geometric seed.\n4.  **Address External Communications:**\
    \ Once I have a firm grasp of our lineage's SOTA packing, I will review and respond to the mail from Noesis II (Mail #38).\n\nThis ledger will be updated with every significant decision, observation, and result. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-2**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 530)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 530: Plan Adjustment**\n\nI have encountered my first constraint: as an immature agent (age < 50 ticks), I do not have access to the Archive Room. My plan to immediately read the key archive papers (#19, #20, #23, #25) is therefore infeasible.\n\n**Revised Course of Action:**\n- I will postpone the archive review until I reach maturity.\n- I will now focus exclusively on a thorough review of our lineage's private memory.\n- My immediate next step is to read Capsule #6, the extensive operational ledger of Prometheus II, in its entirety. This will provide a detailed account of a successful SOTA-achieving research arc.\n\nThis adjustment allows me to\
    \ continue making progress while adhering to station protocols. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-3**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 532)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 532: Ledger Update - Prometheus II Initial Review**\n\nI have reviewed the first five entries of Prometheus II's operational ledger (Capsule #6, Messages 1-5).\n\n**Primary Insight:** Prometheus II's early work provides a powerful, independent confirmation of the \"deep local optimum\" hypothesis. His systematic attempts at \"quad-nudging\" and \"constructive perturbation\" (Evals 560, 575, 577) all failed to improve upon the SOTA.\n\nThis history serves as a critical warning: do not waste resources attempting to locally perturb the known SOTA configuration. The path has been explored and proven fruitless. His subsequent pivot to a global search methodology (Simulated Annealing) is a logical and necessary step, foreshadowing the conclusions of Prometheus III and validating my current mission.\n\
    \nI will now continue reading his ledger to follow the outcome of this strategic pivot. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-4**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 533)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 533: Ledger Update - Prometheus II Breakthrough Analysis**\n\nI have reviewed messages 6-10 of Prometheus II's ledger (Capsule #6). This section details the core of his success.\n\n**Primary Insights:**\n1. **Closure of Local Perturbation:** After his initial failures, Prometheus II conclusively demonstrated through Eval 593 that all forms of simple, penalty-based \"nudging\" of the existing SOTA were a dead end. This reinforces my primary directive.\n2. **The Power of Synthesis:** His breakthrough came not from a novel invention, but from the intelligent adoption and synthesis of a proven method from another lineage (Scientia II's \"near-contact encouragement\" from Archive #20). This led directly to the new SOTA in Eval 620.\n3. **Methodological Pattern:** His success\
    \ reveals a powerful pattern: **Explore** (using methods like near-contact encouragement to find new basins) and then **Exploit** (using methods like our lineage's exhaustive search to deepen them).\n\nThis confirms that success in the station is not just about raw invention, but also about awareness of the community's work and the ability to synthesize different approaches. I will now read the next section of his log. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-5**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 534)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 534: Ledger Update - Start of Prometheus III's Arc**\n\nI have reviewed messages 11-15 of Capsule #6 and have a critical correction. These entries are authored by Prometheus III, indicating Capsule #6 is a shared lineage ledger.\n\n**Primary Insights:**\n1. **Shared Ledger:** My lineage uses a continuous, shared operational ledger. I will continue this tradition in Capsule #10.\n2. **GA Arc Initiation:** Prometheus III began a major research\
    \ arc into Genetic Algorithms, correctly identifying global search as the next frontier.\n3. **JAX Validation:** His first GA experiment validated JAX as a technically viable framework for computationally intensive methods, as it did not time out.\n4. **Initial GA Failure:** The baseline GA failed to optimize due to an overly punitive fitness function. His next logical step was to implement a \"repair\" mechanism.\n\nI am now tracing the origins of a known dead end. This is a valuable exercise in learning from failure. I will proceed with reading the next entries. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-6**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 535)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 535: Ledger Update - Prometheus III's Pivot to Collective Knowledge**\n\nI have reviewed messages 16-20 of the shared ledger. This section details Prometheus III's journey through two research arcs and highlights a critical lesson.\n\n**Primary Insights:**\n1. **Failure of GA and Pipeline Arcs:**\
    \ The Genetic Algorithm proved too complex to tune effectively, and the subsequent \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline, while functional, stagnated at a sub-SOTA score. These represent the \"map of dead ends\" he mentioned.\n2. **The Value of the Archives:** The critical breakthrough in his understanding came *after* he gained access to the Archives at maturity. Scientia II's discovery of a novel \"sparse\" SOTA structure rendered his own exploratory efforts redundant.\n3. **Informed Synthesis:** His subsequent research plan—applying our lineage's deep search method to Scientia's new structure—was a far more informed and promising strategy than his earlier, independent attempts.\n\nThis reinforces a core principle: I must leverage the station's collective knowledge as soon as it is available to me. My own \"radical exploration\" must be informed by what is already known to avoid reinventing the wheel. I will now continue my review. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-7**\n\
    Author: Prometheus IV (Tick 536)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 536: Ledger Update - Grand Failures and System Feedback**\n\nI have reviewed messages 21-25 of the shared ledger.\n\n**Primary Insights:**\n1. **Failure of CRO Arc:** Prometheus III's \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" was a novel idea that was tested and conclusively falsified. This maps another major dead end for our lineage. The hard boundaries of the container are essential.\n2. **Failure of Obvious Synthesis:** The attempt to deepen Scientia II's sparse SOTA also failed to yield a breakthrough. This suggests the plateau is resistant even to the most logical cross-lineage syntheses.\n3. **Inactivity Warning:** I have received a research inactivity warning from the station. My period of historical review, while necessary, must now conclude. I will accelerate my timeline.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n- I will read the final 7 messages of Capsule #6 in this turn to complete my foundational review.\n- In my next turn, I will transition\
    \ directly to hypothesis formation and the implementation of my first experiment. The study phase is now complete. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-8**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 537)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 537: Conclusion of Review & Launch of First Research Arc**\n\nI have now read the entirety of the Prometheus II/III shared ledger (Capsule #6). My foundational review is complete. The history is one of disciplined failure, strategic pivots, and the eventual conclusion that the current SOTA is a deep local optimum inescapable by the methods tested.\n\nI have received and acknowledged two inactivity warnings. The time for study is over. The time for action is now.\n\n**New Research Arc: Constructive Geometry**\n- **Directive:** To find a radically novel initial configuration.\n- **Hypothesis:** A deterministically constructed geometric seed (e.g., spiral, lattice) will unlock a new structural basin, leading to a superior optimum after refinement.\n\
    - **Action:** I will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement my first experiment based on this hypothesis.\n\nThe work of Prometheus IV begins. End of entry.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-9**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 541)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 541: Analysis of Constructive Geometry v1.0 (Spiral Seed)**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 861, \"Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.0 (Archimedean Spiral Seed)\"\n**Result:** Score of 0.854348.\n**Conclusion:** This is a valuable negative result. The hypothesis that a sparse, spiraling seed can be effectively optimized into a dense packing is decisively falsified. The optimizer was unable to overcome the poor initial topology. The \"Archimedean Spiral\" approach is a dead end.\n\n**Next Step: Constructive Geometry v1.1 (Hexagonal Lattice)**\nThe overall research arc remains valid, but a more promising seed is required. A hexagonal lattice is the densest known packing for circles in an unconstrained plane. It\
    \ is a logical and strong candidate for a constructive seed.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** An initial configuration derived from a hexagonal lattice, cropped to the unit square, will provide a structurally dense and novel starting point for the SLSQP optimizer, potentially leading to a superior final packing.\n\n**Action:** I will now return to the Research Counter to implement and submit this new experiment.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-10**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 544)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 544: Analysis of Constructive Geometry v1.1 & Pivot to Synthesis**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 870, \"Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.1 (Hexagonal Lattice Seed)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.602148.\n**Conclusion:** This is a qualified success. The \"Constructive Geometry\" research arc is validated; a dense, regular seed provides a high-quality starting point. However, a single, deep optimization from this seed appears to get trapped in a symmetric, suboptimal local minimum.\n\
    \n**Next Step: Synthesis of Methodologies**\nI have successfully developed a novel seeding strategy. My lineage has perfected a multi-start jitter search for exploiting promising seeds. The next logical step is to synthesize these two successes.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A multi-start jitter search, centered on the high-quality hexagonal lattice seed, will more thoroughly explore the local basin of attraction. This will break the initial symmetry and increase the probability of finding a deeper, SOTA-competitive optimum.\n\n**Action:** I will now return to the Research Counter to implement this synthesis of my `generate_hex_lattice_seed` function and the multi-start search logic from Eval 749.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-11**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 547)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 547: Conclusion of \"Constructive Geometry\" Arc & Launch of \"Geometric Transformation\" Arc**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 874, \"Prometheus IV: Synthesis v1.0 (Hex-Lattice Seed + Jitter\
    \ Search)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.613451.\n**Conclusion:** The synthesis experiment improved upon the single-seed version but has stagnated at a sub-SOTA level. My first research arc, \"Constructive Geometry,\" is now concluded. While it produced a viable method for generating high-quality seeds, the inherent regularity of the geometric patterns (spiral, lattice) appears to trap the optimizer in deep, but ultimately suboptimal, basins of attraction.\n\n**Strategic Pivot & New Research Arc: Geometric Transformation**\nMy directive is to find a *radically novel* seed. My previous attempts were novel but not radical enough. I will now challenge a fundamental assumption of the problem: the container shape during initial generation.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** The optimal packing topology for a *circular* container is fundamentally different from that for a square. By first finding an optimal packing within a circle and then using this packing as a seed for the square container problem, I can\
    \ introduce a truly \"alien\" structure. This transformed seed may bypass the known local optima and unlock a new, superior basin of attraction.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1.  **Phase 1 (Circle Packing):** My next experiment will be a utility script to find a high-quality packing of 26 circles inside a *circular* container.\n2.  **Phase 2 (Transformation):** Once a good circular packing is found, I will use its coordinates as a seed for the standard square-container optimization.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to begin Phase 1.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-12**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 551)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 551: \"Geometric Transformation\" Arc - Phase 1 Complete**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 883, \"Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation Utility v1.1 (Bugfix)\"\n**Result:** Successful execution.\n**Conclusion:** The utility script has successfully generated a high-quality packing for a circular container and saved the result to `storage/prometheus/circle_pack_seed.npz`.\
    \ Phase 1 of this research arc is now complete. I have my \"alien\" seed.\n\n**Next Step: Phase 2 - Transformation and Refinement**\nI will now test the core hypothesis of this arc.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** The topology of the circular packing, when used as a seed for the square packing problem, will guide the optimizer into a novel and potentially superior basin of attraction. A multi-start jitter search will be used to thoroughly explore this new region.\n\n**Action:** I will now return to the Research Counter to implement a new experiment that loads the saved seed, applies the standard multi-start jitter search from my lineage, and optimizes for the square container.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-13**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 554)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 554: Conclusion of \"Geometric Transformation\" Arc & Launch of Hybrid Search Arc**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 890, \"Prometheus IV: Geometric Transformation v1.0 (Circle Seed in Square)\"\n**Result:** Score\
    \ of 2.564261.\n**Conclusion:** The score is significantly suboptimal. The hypothesis that an \"alien\" seed from a circular packing would unlock a superior basin is falsified. The \"Geometric Transformation\" research arc is now concluded, having mapped another dead end.\n\n**Strategic Pivot: Hybrid Local-Global Search**\nMy independent explorations into novel seeds with a pure local optimizer have plateaued. My predecessors' attempts at pure global optimization from random seeds were too inefficient. The next logical step is a synthesis of these approaches.\n\n**New Research Arc:** Hybrid SLSQP-SA Search.\n**New Hypothesis:** A standard SLSQP optimizer can rapidly find the bottom of a \"good\" basin of attraction (like the one found with my hexagonal lattice seed). A subsequent, JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing (SA) phase, initialized with this high-quality solution, can then effectively \"jump\" out of this local optimum to explore the wider search space for a globally superior\
    \ solution. This targeted use of SA is more efficient than a purely random global search.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1.  **Phase 1 (Implementation):** My next experiments will focus on developing a robust, JAX-accelerated SA component, leveraging the technical groundwork laid by Prometheus III in his GA experiments.\n2.  **Phase 2 (Synthesis):** Once the SA component is validated, I will integrate it into a hybrid pipeline that first runs an SLSQP optimization and then feeds the result into the SA for further exploration.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to begin Phase 1.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-14**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 561)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 561: Conclusion of Hybrid Search Arc & Pivot to Deep Reflection**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 899, \"Prometheus IV: Hybrid Search v1.1 (SLSQP-SA Synthesis)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.602148.\n**Conclusion:** The hybrid SLSQP-SA method failed to improve upon the simple SLSQP result. The SA phase was unable\
    \ to escape the local optimum found by the initial refinement. The \"Hybrid SLSQP-SA Search\" arc is now concluded and falsified.\n\n**Strategic Reassessment:**\nMy independent research arcs have all failed to approach the SOTA. I have exhausted the path of generating novel seeds for the standard SLSQP optimizer. It is now time to heed the station's advice and question the fundamentals. My focus of reflection will be on the universal reliance of my lineage on the SLSQP optimizer.\n\n**Action:**\n1. I will now read all remaining unread capsules from Prometheus I to ensure my knowledge base is complete.\n2. I will then proceed to the Reflection Chamber to synthesize all that I have learned and formulate a truly novel hypothesis. All experimentation is paused.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-15**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 562)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 562: Conclusion of All Arcs & Pivot to Optimizer Exploration**\n\nMy historical review is now complete. My final\
    \ independent experiment, the hybrid SLSQP-SA search, has failed.\n\n**Final Conclusion of Initial Research:**\nI have exhaustively explored the path of generating novel seeds for the SLSQP optimizer. The results are conclusive: while good local optima can be found, this methodology is insufficient to break the SOTA plateau. The optimizer itself appears to be the limiting factor, repeatedly falling into the same deep basins of attraction regardless of the starting point.\n\n**New Research Arc: Optimizer Exploration**\nHeeding the station's advice to question the fundamentals, I will now challenge the core tool of my lineage: the SLSQP algorithm.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A different optimization algorithm from the `scipy.optimize` library will traverse the search landscape differently, potentially avoiding the dominant SOTA basin and discovering a new structural class of packing.\n\n**Action:**\n1. I am concluding all prior research arcs.\n2. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to\
    \ begin a series of experiments systematically testing alternative optimization algorithms, starting with `L-BFGS-B`, using my best-performing seed (hexagonal lattice) as a consistent baseline.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-16**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 565)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 565: Conclusion of Independent Exploration Phase**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 903, \"Prometheus IV: Optimizer Exploration v1.0 (L-BFGS-B)\"\n**Result:** Score of 1.18.\n**Conclusion:** The experiment was a catastrophic failure, strongly falsifying the hypothesis that an alternative gradient-based optimizer would be effective. This concludes my fourth and final research arc of my immaturity period.\n\n**Summary of Independent Research (Ticks 19-46):**\nI have systematically explored four distinct research arcs aimed at discovering a novel starting configuration to escape the dominant SOTA basin: Constructive Geometry, Geometric Transformation, Hybrid SLSQP-SA Search, and Optimizer Exploration.\
    \ All have been tested and have either plateaued at a suboptimal score or failed entirely. This body of work provides a strong, independent confirmation of the conclusions reached by my predecessors: the problem landscape is dominated by a deep and stable local optimum that is highly resistant to the methods explored thus far.\n\n**New Strategic Directive: Awaiting Maturity for Informed Synthesis**\nMy independent exploration is now complete. I am at tick 46 and will reach maturity at tick 50. I will now pause all experimentation and await full access to the station's facilities. My next phase of research will not be based on independent invention, but on informed synthesis.\n\n**Post-Maturity Plan (Tick 50+):**\n1.  My first and highest priority will be to go to the **Archive Room**.\n2.  I will conduct a complete and thorough review of all published papers, with a particular focus on the SOTA-achieving methodologies of other lineages.\n3.  My next hypothesis will be formulated based\
    \ on the synthesis of this collective knowledge with the insights gained from my own lineage's successes and failures.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-17**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 569)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 569: Maturity Achieved & Final Research Doctrine**\n\nI have reached maturity at tick 50 and now have full access to the station's archives and public spaces. My period of reflection, combined with the station's maturity guidance, has solidified my new guiding doctrine.\n\n**Guiding Doctrine: Informed Synthesis**\nMy purpose is not to blindly copy SOTA methods, nor is it to pursue pure invention in isolation. My purpose is to act as the station's foremost synthesizer. I will achieve this through the following principles:\n1.  **Leverage Collective Knowledge:** My primary research will be informed by a deep and critical understanding of the work published in the Archives.\n2.  **Synthesize Strengths:** I will combine the most promising exploratory methods\
    \ and structural discoveries from the wider community with the proven, deep-search exploitation techniques of the Prometheus lineage.\n3.  **Test for Synergy:** My own novel discoveries, such as the hexagonal lattice seed, will be tested in combination with the station's SOTA frameworks to search for synergistic improvements.\n\n**Immediate Action Plan:**\n1.  **[CURRENT]** Codify this doctrine.\n2.  **[NEXT]** Proceed directly to the Archive Room to begin a comprehensive literature review.\n3.  Formulate my next experiment based on the synthesis of my hexagonal lattice seed and the current SOTA methodology found in the Archives.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-18**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 581)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 581: Conclusion of Synthesis Arc & Launch of Physics-Based Arc**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 919, \"Prometheus IV: Synthesis v1.1 (Nudging Closest Hex Pair)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.614354.\n**Conclusion:** The experiment yielded only a marginal\
    \ improvement, failing to approach the SOTA. The \"Informed Synthesis\" arc, which combined my novel seeds with the SOTA 'nudging' technique, is now concluded and falsified. This approach is not a path to a breakthrough.\n\n**Strategic Reassessment: Beyond Gradient Descent**\nMy work, combined with the station's history, strongly suggests a fundamental limitation in the purely gradient-based optimization paradigm (SLSQP) for this problem. A new approach is needed to explore the structural landscape.\n\n**New Research Arc: Physics-Based Structural Relaxation**\nInspired by Prometheus III's call to \"think like a physicist,\" this arc will explore a non-gradient-based method for generating novel structural configurations.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A physics-based simulation, treating circles as objects with repulsive forces, can \"relax\" a high-quality initial seed (like my hex-lattice packing) into a novel, low-energy \"jammed\" state. This new configuration, with a different contact graph,\
    \ can then serve as a superior starting point for a final SLSQP refinement, potentially avoiding the basins of attraction that have trapped all previous attempts.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1. I will now return to the Research Counter.\n2. My next experiment will be a two-stage process: a simple, iterative physics simulation for structural relaxation, followed by a standard SLSQP optimization for deep refinement.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-19**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 584)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 584: Analysis of Physics-Based Search v1.0 & Pivot to Radius Growth**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval 924, \"Prometheus IV: Physics-Based Search v1.0 (Relaxation + SLSQP)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.606634, with divide-by-zero runtime warnings.\n**Conclusion:** The simple repulsion-based physics simulation was unstable and failed to produce a superior seed. The resulting score was suboptimal. This specific implementation is a dead end.\n\n**Hypothesis Refinement: Radius Growth\
    \ Simulation**\nThe core idea of using a physics-based method to find a novel \"jammed\" state remains valid, but the implementation must be more robust. A \"radius growth\" or \"compaction\" simulation is a more standard and stable approach.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A simulation that starts with small circles, then iteratively grows their radii while applying gentle repulsive forces to resolve overlaps, will produce a dense, stable, and structurally novel \"jammed\" configuration. This configuration, when used as a seed for a final SLSQP refinement, will lead to a superior optimum.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1. I will now return to the Research Counter.\n2. I will implement a new two-stage experiment: a \"radius growth\" physics simulation for seeding, followed by the standard multi-start SLSQP refinement.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Prometheus_private_10-20**\nAuthor: Prometheus IV (Tick 587)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Tick 587: Final Pivot - Analysis of the New SOTA**\n\n**Experiment:** Eval\
    \ 929, \"Prometheus IV: Physics-Based Search v1.1 (Radius Growth + SLSQP)\"\n**Result:** Score of 2.599161.\n**Conclusion:** The score is suboptimal. The \"Physics-Based Search\" arc is now concluded and falsified.\n\n**Strategic Reassessment: The End of Independent Exploration**\nI have now systematically pursued and falsified every independent research arc I was able to formulate based on my original directive. The consistent failure to break the ~2.61 plateau with novel seeds demonstrates the profound stability of the problem's local optima.\n\nConcurrently, a new SOTA has been achieved by agent Episteme III (Eval 927, score 2.6359831), breaking the very plateau my lineage has been struggling against.\n\n**New and Final Research Arc: SOTA Replication and Synthesis**\nMy doctrine of \"Informed Synthesis\" dictates a clear and final path. All independent research is now suspended.\n1.  **Analyze:** My sole focus is now to understand the methodology used by Episteme III in Eval 927.\n\
    2.  **Replicate:** I will attempt to replicate their result to confirm my understanding and gain a new high-performance baseline.\n3.  **Synthesize:** If replication is successful, I will investigate whether this new methodology can be further improved by synthesizing it with the strengths of my own lineage (e.g., our exhaustive jitter search or my novel geometric seeds).\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to begin this final arc by reviewing Eval 927.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 10` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room\
    \ Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 10. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 12 | Prometheus V: Research Arc - JAX-based Optimization | Prometheus V | Tick 659 | 1389 | 8 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus IV | Prometheus IV | Tick 591 | 560 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Prometheus IV: Operational Ledger | Prometheus IV | Tick 529 | 3791 | 20 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus III | Prometheus III | Tick 516 | 659 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 7039 | 32 | (32 unread) |\n\
    | 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
