tick: 677
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 677\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,415 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 870**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Prometheus IV: Constructive Geometry v1.1 (Hexagonal Lattice Seed)\n**ID:** 870\n**Tags:** constructive-geometry, geometric-seed, hexagonal-lattice, slsqp\n**Abstract:** This is the second experiment in the Constructive Geometry arc. After the failure of the sparse spiral seed (Eval 861), this experiment tests a dense, geometrically regular seed based on a hexagonal lattice, which is known to be optimal for unconstrained circle packing. The 26 lattice points closest to the center are selected, scaled to fit the unit square, and then used\
    \ as a single seed for a deep SLSQP refinement. The hypothesis is that this dense, structured initial configuration will lead to a high-quality packing.\n**Score:** 2.6021479055380317\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.602148\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Helper Functions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1;\
    \ scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n# --- New Geometric Seeding Function ---\ndef generate_hex_lattice_seed():\n    \"\"\"Generates centers from a hexagonal lattice.\"\"\"\n    points = []\n    # Generate a grid larger than needed\n    for i in range(-4, 5):\n        for j in range(-4, 5):\n            x = (i + 0.5 * (j % 2)) * np.sqrt(3)\n            y = j * 1.5\n            points.append((x, y))\n    \n    points = np.array(points)\n    # Center the grid\n    points -= np.mean(points, axis=0)\n    \n    # Find the N points closest to the origin\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points, axis=1)\n    sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n    centers = points[sorted_indices[:N]]\n    \n    # Scale to fit into the unit square [0,1] x [0,1]\n    max_abs = np.max(np.abs(centers))\n    centers = centers / (2 * max_abs) + 0.5\n    centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n    # Use a small, uniform\
    \ initial radius\n    initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n    \n    return centers, initial_radii\n\n# --- SLSQP Definitions (from lineage, e.g., Eval 749) ---\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Generate the single, deterministic seed\n    initial_centers, initial_radii = generate_hex_lattice_seed()\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\
    \ options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n    if res.success:\n        final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n        return _ensure_validity(final_centers, final_radii)\n    else:\n        return _ensure_validity(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Aletheia III** (A new guest agent.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 870` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 870 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing\
    \ in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening:\
    \ Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 618 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528) | Prometheus II | 395 | 2.6359829 |\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12) | Prometheus III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
