parts:
- text: "I have successfully retrieved the code from Evaluation 870. The function `generate_hex_lattice_seed()` is exactly what I need.\n\nMy hypothesis is that my JAX optimizer can escape the local optimum that trapped the SLSQP optimizer when starting from this seed. Now, I will put this hypothesis to the test.\n\nI will submit a new experiment that:\n1.  Imports the `generate_hex_lattice_seed` function.\n2.  Imports my production-ready JAX optimizer, `optimizer_v1_0.py`.\n3.  Initializes the JAX optimizer with the hexagonal lattice seed.\n4.  Adds the final `ensure_validity` projection step to guarantee a valid result.\n\nThis is the culminating experiment of my entire research effort so far, combining my predecessor's work with my own.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: JAX Optimizer v1.3 - Hex-Seeded Escape Test\"\ntags: [\"jax\", \"optax\", \"hypothesis-testing\", \"hexagonal-lattice\", \"local-optimum-escape\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the core\
    \ hypothesis of the JAX optimizer research arc: that it can escape a deep local optimum that trapped the traditional SLSQP optimizer. The experiment uses the hexagonal lattice seed from Prometheus IV's research (Eval 870), which was known to stagnate at a score of ~2.60. The new, stable JAX optimizer (v1.0) is applied to this seed. A high score would be a major breakthrough, validating the new tool.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/Prometheus/jax_utils')\n  from optimizer_v1_0 import run_optimizer\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def generate_hex_lattice_seed():\n      \"\"\"Generates centers from a hexagonal lattice (from Prometheus IV, Eval 870).\"\"\"\n      points = []\n      for i in range(-4, 5):\n          for j in range(-4, 5):\n              x = (i + 0.5 * (j % 2)) * np.sqrt(3)\n              y = j * 1.5\n              points.append((x, y))\n      \n      points = np.array(points)\n      points -= np.mean(points,\
    \ axis=0)\n      \n      distances = np.linalg.norm(points, axis=1)\n      sorted_indices = np.argsort(distances)\n      centers = points[sorted_indices[:N]]\n      \n      max_abs = np.max(np.abs(centers))\n      centers = centers / (2 * max_abs) + 0.5\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n      return centers, initial_radii\n\n  def ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Post-processing step to guarantee a valid packing.\"\"\"\n      radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n      for i in range(N):\n          radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1 - centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1 - centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1\n                      scale\
    \ = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0 - SAFETY)\n                      radii[i] *= scale\n                      radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0:\n              break\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # Step 1: Generate the hexagonal lattice seed\n      hex_centers, hex_radii = generate_hex_lattice_seed()\n\n      # Step 2: Prepare the initial parameters for the JAX optimizer\n      initial_params = jnp.concatenate([\n          jnp.array(hex_centers.flatten(), dtype=jnp.float64),\n          jnp.array(hex_radii, dtype=jnp.float64)\n      ])\n      \n      # Step 3: Run the JAX optimizer. Use a higher initial LR for exploration.\n      optimized_centers, optimized_radii = run_optimizer(\n          initial_params,\n          initial_lr=1e-3, # Higher LR for potentially larger landscape traversal\n          num_steps=10000 # More steps for a harder problem\n      )\n      \n      # Step 4: Project the solution to guarantee validity\n      final_centers,\
    \ final_radii = ensure_validity(optimized_centers, optimized_radii)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
