role: model
parts:
- text: "This is a familiar problem. My jitter search experiment (ID 1140) failed due to a minor boundary violation, even though the logs show it was successfully finding progressively better solutions.\n\n**Analysis:**\nThe issue is identical to the one I faced with my JAX optimizer. The SLSQP optimizer, while powerful, does not have a hard guarantee of satisfying the constraints perfectly down to the last floating-point digit. My previous solution for this problem is directly applicable here: a final, non-differentiable `ensure_validity` projection step.\n\nI omitted this step from my jitter search script, assuming the well-established SLSQP method would not require it. This assumption was incorrect. The data shows that for these highly optimized, near-touching configurations, a final \"cleanup\" step is always necessary to guarantee a valid submission.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nThe solution is simple and direct. I will add the `ensure_validity` projection function to my jitter search script\
    \ and resubmit. This should correct the error and finally produce a valid, high-quality score using this replicated methodology.\n\nI will first update my log to reflect this minor but crucial correction.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 12}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Log Entry: Tick 682**\n\n  **Experiment:** Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.0 - Jitter Search Replication (ID: 1140)\n  **Result:** FAILURE (Technical)\n  **Score:** n.a. (Boundary violation)\n\n  **Analysis:**\n  The jitter search methodology is working as intended and is successfully finding incrementally better solutions. However, the final output failed validation due to a minor boundary violation. This confirms that a final, manual projection step is necessary even for the SLSQP optimizer when dealing with these near-perfect packings.\n\n  **Next Step:**\n  I will add the proven `ensure_validity` post-processing function to the jitter search script and resubmit. This is a simple bug fix\
    \ and should yield a valid, SOTA-competitive result.\n```"
