role: model
parts:
- text: "The log is updated. Now to execute the corrected experiment. I will return to the Research Counter and submit the jitter search script again, this time with the crucial `ensure_validity` function added to guarantee a valid final packing.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.1 - Jitter Search (with Projection)\"\ntags: [\"sota-push\", \"jitter-search\", \"multi-start\", \"slsqp\", \"projection\", \"bugfix\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix submission for the jitter search methodology (see Eval 1140). The previous version failed due to a minor boundary violation. This version adds the `ensure_validity` post-processing function, which manually projects the final solution to guarantee all constraints are met. This should produce a valid, SOTA-competitive result.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY\
    \ = 1e-9\n\n  # --- Helper Functions ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  # --- SLSQP Definitions ---\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1) + 1e-12)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  # --- ADDED: Post-processing Projection Function ---\n  def ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n      for i in range(N):\n          radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1 - centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1 - centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(5):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n \
    \                 dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); radii[i]*=scale; radii[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # --- Data Loading ---\n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          return np.loadtxt(centers_path), np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n      except Exception: return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      base_centers, base_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if base_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      best_score = -1.0\n      best_packing = (base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      jitter_amplitude = 1e-4\n      num_restarts = 40 # Increased restarts for a more thorough search\n\n \
    \     bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for i in range(num_restarts):\n          np.random.seed(int(time.time()*1000) + i) # More precise seeding\n          \n          jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amplitude, jitter_amplitude, size=base_centers.shape)\n          perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, base_radii)\n          \n          res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n              c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n              current_score = np.sum(r)\n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  print(f\"Run {i+1}: New best score found: {current_score}\")\n                  best_score = current_score\n       \
    \           best_packing = (c, r)\n\n      # --- Apply final validity projection to the best found packing ---\n      final_centers, final_radii = ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
