parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 684\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 109,858 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 43 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.1 - Jitter Search (with Projection)' (ID: 1143) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.635977392111827\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1143\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the random seed overflow error. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.636.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code\
    \ attempted to use `int(time.time()*1000) + i` as a seed value for `np.random.seed()`.\n\nThe problem:\n- `time.time()` returns the current Unix timestamp in seconds (e.g., ~1.7 billion in 2025)\n- Multiplying by 1000 gives milliseconds (~1.7 trillion)\n- NumPy's random seed must be between 0 and 2^32 - 1 (approximately 4.3 billion)\n- The calculated seed value far exceeded this limit, causing a ValueError\n\nError message:\n```\nValueError: Seed must be between 0 and 2**32 - 1\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 65 in the original submission from:\n```python\nnp.random.seed(int(time.time()*1000) + i)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nnp.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n```\n\nThe modulo operation (`% (2**32)`) ensures the seed value always stays within the valid range [0, 2^32 - 1].\n\n## Result\n- Code executed successfully without crashes\n- Achieved score: **2.635977392111827**\n- The algorithm performed 40 restarts with jittered initial conditions as intended\n- The fix\
    \ maintains the original intent of varying random seeds across restarts while ensuring validity\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Helper Functions ---\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n# --- SLSQP Definitions ---\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1) + 1e-12)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\
    \n# --- ADDED: Post-processing Projection Function ---\ndef ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n    radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n    for i in range(N):\n        radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1 - centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1 - centers[i,1])\n    for _ in range(5):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); radii[i]*=scale; radii[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return centers, radii\n\n# --- Data Loading ---\ndef load_sota_data():\n    centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n    radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n    try:\n        return np.loadtxt(centers_path), np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n    except Exception: return None, None\n\ndef construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n    base_centers, base_radii = load_sota_data()\n    if base_centers is None:\n        return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    best_score = -1.0\n    best_packing = (base_centers, base_radii)\n\n    jitter_amplitude = 1e-4\n    num_restarts = 40 # Increased restarts for a more thorough search\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    for i in range(num_restarts):\n        # FIX: Ensure seed stays within valid range (0 to 2^32 - 1)\n        np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amplitude, jitter_amplitude, size=base_centers.shape)\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n        initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, base_radii)\n\n        res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol':\
    \ 1e-9})\n\n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n            c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n            current_score = np.sum(r)\n            if current_score > best_score:\n                print(f\"Run {i+1}: New best score found: {current_score}\")\n                best_score = current_score\n                best_packing = (c, r)\n\n    # --- Apply final validity projection to the best found packing ---\n    final_centers, final_radii = ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nRun 1: New best score found: 2.6359773947801357\nRun 2: New best score found: 2.6359773947804497\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally\
    \ refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.1 - Jitter Search (with Projection)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1143.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2:\
    \ Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 618 | 1 | Utility: Identify Near-Contacts in Scientia II SOTA Packing (Eval 528) | Prometheus II | 395 | 2.6359829 |\n| 816 | 1 | Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12) | Prometheus\
    \ III | 514 | 2.6359774 |\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
