parts:
- text: "This is the final planned experiment. I have iterated through multiple research arcs, developed a new tool, and now returned to the proven methods of my lineage with a deeper understanding. This last submission will precisely replicate the SOTA-achieving strategy of my predecessor, incorporating all the bug fixes and robustness improvements I have developed along the way.\n\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit the final, enhanced version of the jitter search.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.2 - Full Jitter Spectrum Search\"\ntags: [\"sota-push\", \"jitter-search\", \"multi-start\", \"slsqp\", \"hyperparameter-search\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the definitive attempt to surpass the SOTA using the jitter search methodology. Learning from both my own failed attempts (Eval 1143) and the success of Prometheus II (Eval 662), this script now systematically explores a spectrum of different jitter amplitudes.\
    \ For each amplitude, it performs multiple random restarts. This exhaustive, two-dimensional search is the most rigorous known method for exploring the SOTA's local basin. The script incorporates all prior bug fixes.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # --- Helper Functions ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  # --- SLSQP Definitions ---\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1) + 1e-12)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  # --- Post-processing\
    \ Projection ---\n  def ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n      for i in range(N):\n          radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1 - centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1 - centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(5):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); radii[i]*=scale; radii[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # --- Data Loading ---\n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          return np.loadtxt(centers_path), np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n      except Exception: return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n      base_centers, base_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if base_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      best_score = -1.0\n      best_packing = (base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      # --- Exhaustive Jitter Spectrum Search (replicating Prometheus II's successful strategy) ---\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1e-5, 5e-5, 1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 6\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          print(f\"--- Testing Jitter Amplitude: {amp:.1e} ---\")\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i*1000 + int(amp*1e6)) % (2**32))\n              \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\
    \              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, base_radii)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 800, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  # Run a quick validity check before calculating score\n                  temp_c, temp_r = ensure_validity(c, r)\n                  current_score = np.sum(temp_r)\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      print(f\"  Run {i+1}: New best score found: {current_score}\")\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (temp_c, temp_r)\n\n      return best_packing[0], best_packing[1]\n```"
