tick: 687
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is it. All my research, all the failed hypotheses and incremental successes, have led to this final, data-driven attempt. The logs from my previous experiment clearly showed a path forward: more aggressive and thorough searching. I will now execute this final experiment.\n\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit my most exhaustive search yet.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus V: SOTA Deepening v1.3 - Final Exhaustive Search\"\ntags: [\"sota-push\", \"jitter-search\", \"exhaustive-search\", \"slsqp\", \"hyperparameter-search\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the final and most exhaustive attempt of this research arc to achieve a new SOTA. Based on logs from Eval 1146 showing that larger jitters were more effective, this submission significantly expands the search space. It tests a wider and more aggressive range of jitter amplitudes (up to 5e-3) and increases the number of restarts per amplitude for a more thorough exploration\
    \ of the SOTA basin.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # --- Helper Functions ---\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  # --- SLSQP Definitions ---\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1) + 1e-12)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  # --- Post-processing Projection ---\n  def ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n      for i in range(N):\n          radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1 - centers[i,0], centers[i,1],\
    \ 1 - centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(5):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); radii[i]*=scale; radii[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # --- Data Loading ---\n  def load_sota_data():\n      centers_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/centers.txt'\n      radii_path = 'storage/Prometheus/sota_baseline/radii.txt'\n      try:\n          return np.loadtxt(centers_path), np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n      except Exception: return None, None\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      base_centers, base_radii = load_sota_data()\n      if base_centers is None:\n          return np.zeros((N, 2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      best_score = -1.0\n      best_packing =\
    \ (base_centers, base_radii)\n      \n      # --- Final Exhaustive Jitter Spectrum Search ---\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\n      restarts_per_amplitude = 8\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n          print(f\"--- Testing Jitter Amplitude: {amp:.1e} ---\")\n          for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n              np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i*1000 + int(amp*1e6)) % (2**32))\n              \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, base_radii)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 800, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\
    \              \n              if res.success:\n                  c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  temp_c, temp_r = ensure_validity(c, r)\n                  current_score = np.sum(temp_r)\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      print(f\"  Run {i+1}: New best score found: {current_score}\")\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_packing = (temp_c, temp_r)\n\n      return best_packing[0], best_packing[1]\n```"
thinking_content: '**Final Push for SOTA: Exhaustive Jitter Search**


  Okay, here''s the plan. I''m ready to run this final experiment. The goal is clear: push the state-of-the-art further with a more exhaustive jitter search. I''ve analyzed the previous results (Eval 1146), and it''s obvious that larger jitter amplitudes were the key to progress. So, I''m going to expand the search space significantly.


  First, I''ll head back to the Research Counter. Then, I''ll submit a new experiment. This will be a modification of `ID 1146`, but with some key changes. I''m going to expand the `jitter_amplitudes` list to include even larger values. I''m thinking of incorporating `3e-3`, `4e-3`, and `5e-3` now. I will also increase `restarts_per_amplitude` to be more thorough, making sure I''m really covering the ground here.


  Previously I had `jitter_amplitudes = [1e-5, 5e-5, 1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3]` and `restarts_per_amplitude = 6`. This resulted in a total of 36 runs. Now, I will update it to `jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]` and `restarts_per_amplitude = 8`. This gives a new total of 56 runs - a significant increase. It will be a more demanding experiment, but the potential payoff is worth it. I am very confident that these parameters will lead us closer to achieving the optimal solution.


  The code itself will be almost identical, just modifying those two key lines. I''m ready to execute the action sequence: `/execute_action{goto research}` followed by `/execute_action{submit 1}` with the YAML. It''s time to generate the submission YAML file. Let''s make this the defining result.

  '
