- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 695\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus V\n- Agent Description: Advancing the SOTA by direct replication or by innovating the core optimizer.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 137,197 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 827**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14)\n**ID:** 827\n**Tags:** utility, data extraction, sota, n=26, structural analysis\n**Abstract:** This utility script re-executes the optimization logic of Quest II's SOTA-achieving nudged submission (Evaluation ID 824) and explicitly prints the resulting best circle centers and radii to STDOUT. The purpose is to accurately extract the precise numerical data of this packing, which originated from encouraging near-contact pair (8,14), for subsequent detailed structural analysis\
    \ and comparison, in order to verify if it represents a novel structural class.\n**Score:** 2.6359830849175325\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9 \nTOL = 1e-9 # Corrected: Define TOL here as it's used in the code\n\n# Path to Quest II's SOTA packing (from Eval ID 820)\nSOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota'\nSOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'centers.txt')\nSOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Nudging Parameters (used for single-step perturbation)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP = 5e1 \nEPS_CLOSE_STEP = 0.005 \n\n# Targeted pair for encouragement\nTARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE = (8, 14) \n\n# Prometheus II's Multi-start SLSQP parameters (from Eval ID 662)\nSLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1e-4,\
    \ 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\nSLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5\nSLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS = len(SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES) * SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE\n\n# --- Helper functions ---\ndef load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load baseline SOTA data. {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef objective_slsqp(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n\
    \    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): \n        r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    \n    for _ in range(10): \n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum: \n                    violations+=1\n                    scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY) \n                    r[i]*=scale\n                    r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: \n            break \n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0) \n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    print(\"Starting Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824.\")\n    \n    base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II, SOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II)\n    \n    if base_sota_centers is None:\n        print(\"Error: Could\
    \ not load base SOTA packing. Returning safe fallback.\")\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Generate Nudged Seed (Structural Discovery) ---\n    print(f\"--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} ---\")\n    \n    i_enc, j_enc = TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE\n    \n    dist_enc_vec = base_sota_centers[i_enc] - base_sota_centers[j_enc]\n    dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(dist_enc_vec)\n    slack_enc = dist_enc - (base_sota_radii[i_enc] + base_sota_radii[j_enc])\n\n    current_nudged_centers = np.copy(base_sota_centers)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.copy(base_sota_radii)\n\n    if dist_enc > TOL and (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) > 0:\n        grad_dist_enc_ci = dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n        grad_dist_enc_cj = -dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n\n        move_amount_centers = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.01 \n        current_nudged_centers[i_enc] += grad_dist_enc_ci\
    \ * move_amount_centers\n        current_nudged_centers[j_enc] += grad_dist_enc_cj * move_amount_centers\n\n        move_amount_radii = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.001 \n        current_nudged_radii[i_enc] += move_amount_radii\n        current_nudged_radii[j_enc] += move_amount_radii\n    else:\n        print(f\"  Nudging penalty for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} not active or circles coincident. Applying default small jitter.\")\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-1e-4, 1e-4, size=base_sota_centers.shape)\n        current_nudged_centers = base_sota_centers + jitter\n        current_nudged_radii = base_sota_radii \n\n    current_nudged_centers = np.clip(current_nudged_centers, R_MIN, 1.0 - R_MIN)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.clip(current_nudged_radii, R_MIN, 0.5)\n    nudged_centers, nudged_radii = _ensure_validity(current_nudged_centers, current_nudged_radii)\n    \n    print(f\"  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): {np.sum(nudged_radii):.6f}\"\
    )\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (Prometheus II's style) ---\n    print(f\"\\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement ({SLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS} restarts) ---\")\n    \n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    bounds_slsqp = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints_slsqp = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    for amp in SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for i in range(SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 1000 \n            np.random.seed(seed)\n            \n            jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=nudged_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(nudged_centers + jitter, R_MIN, 1 - R_MIN) \n            initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, nudged_radii)\n            \n            print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE} (Jitter: {amp:.3e},\
    \ Seed: {seed})\")\n            \n            res = minimize(objective_slsqp, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds_slsqp, constraints=constraints_slsqp, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n            \n            if res.success:\n                current_score = -res.fun\n                c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                final_restart_score = np.sum(r_final)\n\n                print(f\"    Restart successful. Final score: {final_restart_score:.6f}\")\n                if final_restart_score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = final_restart_score\n                    best_overall_centers = c_final\n                    best_overall_radii = r_final\n                    print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"    Restart failed: {res.message}\")\n\n    print(f\"Final best score after all restarts: {best_overall_score:.6f}\"\
    )\n\n    if best_overall_centers is not None:\n        print(\"\\n--- BEGIN BEST_CENTERS ---\")\n        np.savetxt(sys.stdout, best_overall_centers, fmt='%.18e')\n        print(\"--- END BEST_CENTERS ---\")\n        print(\"\\n--- BEGIN BEST_RADII ---\")\n        np.savetxt(sys.stdout, best_overall_radii, fmt='%.18e')\n        print(\"--- END BEST_RADII ---\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: No best packing found. Returning initial nudged base packing.\")\n        return nudged_centers, nudged_radii\n\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824.\n--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair (8, 14) ---\n  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): 2.630517\n\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (35 restarts) ---\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1100)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n\
    \    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1101)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1102)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1103)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1104)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1500)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1501)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1502)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1503)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP\
    \ Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1504)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter:\
    \ 2.000e-03, Seed: 3003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter:\
    \ 4.000e-03, Seed: 5003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\nFinal best score after all restarts: 2.635983\n\n--- BEGIN BEST_CENTERS ---\n8.463950069577350077e-02 8.463950069577429181e-02\n1.302211010652277456e-01 2.946094887818287988e-01\n7.886037291596376120e-02 4.972844462041109415e-01\n1.332585727708140988e-01 7.023095250891661090e-01\n8.492626245489670600e-02 9.150737375451013511e-01\n\
    2.747832833508203620e-01 1.067901446285782902e-01\n3.869235534095998852e-01 2.947460590489513477e-01\n2.753426167714411177e-01 4.955317606743629422e-01\n3.816658444526481730e-01 7.026096036990244764e-01\n2.739528396239501729e-01 8.948174397312549377e-01\n4.846008026519154077e-01 1.030605201415831784e-01\n5.976347963876610381e-01 2.716298514860021607e-01\n5.299634197531921664e-01 4.986680755034036960e-01\n5.960427019081369071e-01 7.269057143115960073e-01\n4.825955822105365001e-01 8.965327666420513930e-01\n6.832585349730804225e-01 9.573232930702131604e-02\n7.636735693833850425e-01 2.397105279275375811e-01\n7.424170495016374494e-01 4.033587836026811257e-01\n7.420494434605916512e-01 5.952197329397319603e-01\n6.820800429325920566e-01 9.038486659542352974e-01\n8.892209872092854406e-01 1.107790127907171684e-01\n9.076084484290416476e-01 3.131158099704025588e-01\n9.060726627225563767e-01 4.994283691390392077e-01\n9.074079050485647224e-01 6.859430219867849177e-01\n8.888438205895565769e-01 8.888438205895565769e-01\n\
    7.629588636539990087e-01 7.593524015609310895e-01\n--- END BEST_CENTERS ---\n\n--- BEGIN BEST_RADII ---\n8.463950069577065582e-02\n1.302211010652227496e-01\n7.886037291596070808e-02\n1.332585727708087975e-01\n8.492626245489523495e-02\n1.067901446285765693e-01\n1.120770889502566564e-01\n1.176296880465369787e-01\n1.151488801600176887e-01\n1.051825602687450623e-01\n1.030605201415807221e-01\n9.989835059275367635e-02\n1.370104301237446698e-01\n1.006003678187085831e-01\n1.034672333579485654e-01\n9.573232930701848498e-02\n6.918067635723218478e-02\n9.584232574550309580e-02\n9.601897575825041331e-02\n9.615133404576176046e-02\n1.107790127907128386e-01\n9.239155157095628457e-02\n9.392733727744070893e-02\n9.259209495143277957e-02\n1.111561794104418410e-01\n6.944019371125496887e-02\n--- END BEST_RADII ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `review 827`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 827 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication\
    \ of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 117 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-117, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\
    \n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
