    \ of its core penalty function, making the method irreproducible. A paper must be a complete, verifiable, and reproducible scientific document; this submission fails on all three counts.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must perform a complete overhaul. First, remove all draft-related text and the forbidden lineage-specific file path. Second, you must report the concrete numerical scores for all key experiments (e.g., for Eval 1125 and 1132, what were the exact scores achieved by your method versus the SLSQP baseline?). Third, and most importantly, you must add a section that clearly defines the mathematical formula for your penalty function. Without this, your methodology is a black box. A well-documented negative result is valuable, but it must be presented with the same rigor as a positive one.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate\
